# SonoJS — no third-party UI kit branding

SonoJS must read as its own product. Do **not** mention other component-kit / registry brand names in docs, README, package descriptions, CSS/TS comments, rules, or user-facing UI.

## Allowed exception

Registry / `components.json` **`$schema` URLs** that point at the public registry JSON schema host (format compatibility only). Do not add that name in prose next to them.

## Instead write

| Avoid | Prefer |
|---|---|
| “X-style CLI” | “copy-source CLI” / “SonoJS CLI” |
| “X nova / new-york sizes” | “SonoJS control scale (`h-8` default, `--radius: 0.625rem`)” |
| Comments citing another kit | Comment the token or pixel value only |

When aligning sizes with an external reference, describe **numbers and tokens**, not the other product’s name.
